- Story & Context: Huddled within the dripping access chamber of the Nordkreuz Interchange, synth-weaver Lise smeared pulverized charcoal and graphite grease down her neck to keep from freezing while the shudder of five thousand idling diesel engines rattled the concrete against her spine. Weeping from exhaustion and tear gas seep, she patched her string synthesizer's highest octave lead into the walk-signal audio actuator, turning the rhythmic pedestrian warning chimes into an excruciating, weeping baroque chorale that carried for miles down the valley. A patrol officer fired three beanbag rounds through the maintenance grate, denting her synth chassis and spraying her forearm with hot copper shrapnel, but she clamped her jaw tight and doubled her tempo without missing a chord. Pressing her bleeding brow against the live junction housing, she howled her confession into the open conduit, "wrap my bones in bitumen until the wings tear through," permanently frying the automated interchange processor with an intentional saltwater short.
